\f0\b\fs48 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 VHSart \'97 Dark-Field Horizontal Luma Speckles & Streaks\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Objective\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Implement a dedicated VHSart preset that reconstructs the supplied reference video, 
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 video_1.mov
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2  (~1.0 second).\
The effect consists of intermittent monochrome horizontal speckles, short streaks, and signal-dropout-like fragments distributed over a predominantly black or very dark background.\
Its defining characteristics are:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Dark-field appearance with scattered white and light-gray details.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Horizontal speckles and short irregular streaks.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Higher noise density toward the upper part of the frame.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Medium, variable density across the remaining frame.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Noticeable frame-to-frame changes in speckle positions and overall density.\
{\listtext	\'95	}No significant chromatic noise or RGB displacement.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The effect must be entirely procedural inside the native C++ After Effects plugin. Do not use pre-rendered images, video, GIFs, stock textures, or external overlays.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Reference watermark:
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  The faint 
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 videohive
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2  watermark is part of the supplied reference footage, not part of the effect. Do not reproduce, generate, or incorporate it into the plugin.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 1. Inspect Existing VHSart Engines First\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Before implementing anything, thoroughly inspect the existing project and identify the available:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Static and signal-noise generators.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Monochrome/luminance noise processing.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Horizontal speckle and segment generation.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Tracking dropout and horizontal interference systems.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Noise density and spatial distribution controls.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Temporal modulation and deterministic seed systems.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Input blending and alpha compositing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Prefer a dedicated preset configured through existing VHSart engines.\
If the existing systems already support the required appearance, reuse them. If specific functionality is missing, extend the most appropriate existing engine instead of creating a redundant standalone engine.\
The main potential extensions are:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}Vertical density weighting toward the top.\
{\listtext	2.	}Independent horizontal speckle stretching.\
{\listtext	3.	}Frame-to-frame density modulation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Preserve all existing effects, presets, controls, and rendering behavior.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 2. Primary Component \'97 Dark-Field Horizontal Luma Speckles & Streaks\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Generate irregular monochrome speckles and horizontal fragments over a predominantly dark field.\
Visual requirements:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Predominantly black or very dark background.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Scattered white, light-gray, and occasional medium-gray details.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Small horizontal particles with variable lengths.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Short, interrupted horizontal lines.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Irregular spacing and distribution.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Medium density overall, with localized higher-density regions.\
{\listtext	\'95	}No large continuous bands.\
{\listtext	\'95	}No full-frame bright static.\
{\listtext	\'95	}No colored noise or noticeable chromatic separation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The noise should resemble intermittent analog signal interference or horizontal signal dropouts on a dark television screen.\
Maintain a convincing balance between empty dark regions and scattered illuminated details.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 3. Secondary Component \'97 Top-Weighted Density Distribution\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 The reference has a noticeably denser concentration of bright speckles and horizontal fragments near the upper edge.\
Implement a controllable vertical density distribution.\
Requirements:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Noise remains distributed across the entire frame.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Density gradually increases toward the top.\
{\listtext	\'95	}The transition must be smooth and irregular, not a sharply separated horizontal band.\
{\listtext	\'95	}The lower portion remains darker and generally less dense.\
{\listtext	\'95	}The top-density influence must be independently adjustable.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Do not create a hard boundary between upper and lower regions.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Use a normalized vertical coordinate and a configurable density-weighting function.\
The top-density effect should modify the probability of generating speckles, not simply brighten the top of the image.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 4. Horizontal Speckle and Segment Generation\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Use a deterministic procedural hash or equivalent fast random-generation method.\
Generate variable horizontal segments using:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Horizontal position.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Vertical position.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Segment length.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Segment brightness.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Segment thickness.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Local density probability.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Temporal seed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The horizontal structures should be small and irregular.\
Support a controllable 
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 Horizontal Stretch
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2  parameter that changes the actual length of the generated particles and fragments.\
Do not implement this control as global image scaling, blur, or geometric stretching.\
Avoid:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Circular or isotropic grain.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Large rectangular blocks.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Regular repeating grids.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Long continuous scanlines.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Thick tracking bands.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Unrelated geometric distortion.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 5. Temporal Density Variation\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 The reference demonstrates a visible density difference between the observed frames:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}At 00:00.000, the upper region and overall distribution appear denser.\
{\listtext	\'95	}At 00:00.500, the overall density is relatively reduced and the noise positions have changed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Implement independent temporal modulation for:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}Speckle positions.\
{\listtext	2.	}Segment lengths.\
{\listtext	3.	}Local brightness.\
{\listtext	4.	}Overall frame density.\
{\listtext	5.	}Upper-region density.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Provide a 
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 Frame Density Variation
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2  parameter to control how much the total number of generated speckles changes over time.\
The temporal behavior must be intermittent and irregular rather than periodic or mechanically pulsing.\
Do not hardcode the observed density difference to the exact timestamps. Use a deterministic temporal system driven by the frame/time and user seed.\
Provide:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls10\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Animate With Time: On/Off.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Frame Density Variation.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Animation Speed.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Random Seed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 When animation is disabled, the complete pattern and its density distribution must remain frozen.\
Identical seed and frame/time inputs must always generate identical output.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 6. Monochrome Luma Architecture\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 The effect must remain monochrome.\
Use equal generated RGB values:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 R = G = B = Luma
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 \
The generated details should use white and grayscale values over a dark background.\
Do not introduce:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}RGB channel displacement.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Saturated red, green, blue, or magenta noise.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Chroma smearing.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Color bleeding.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Rainbow interference.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Chromatic tracking artifacts.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The effect should operate primarily in the luminance domain.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 7. Procedural Algorithm\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Use separate deterministic random streams or decorrelated hash inputs for the base speckles, horizontal segments, and temporal density modulation.\
A suitable conceptual structure is:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 A. Temporal Seed
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
Calculate an effective seed from the user seed and the current frame/time.\

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 B. Spatial Density
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
Calculate local speckle probability using:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls12\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Base speckle density.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Top-density weighting.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Frame-density modulation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Conceptually:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 density(x, y, t) = baseDensity \'d7 topWeight(y) \'d7 frameVariation(t)
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 \
Ensure the result is clamped to a valid probability range.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 C. Segment Generation
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
Partition the horizontal dimension into variable-length segments.\
Use a deterministic hash of segment coordinates, row position, and temporal seed to determine:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls13\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Whether a segment is generated.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Its length.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Its luminance.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Its thickness.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 D. Luminance Output
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
Generate monochrome values and composite them using the selected output mode.\
Keep the top-density weighting separate from brightness modulation: increasing density must create more illuminated elements, not merely make existing elements brighter.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 8. Input and Compositing Modes\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Support two operating modes:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Generated Dark-Field Signal
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls14\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Generate a predominantly black background.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Add procedural monochrome speckles and horizontal streaks.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Allow the result to function independently as a complete signal texture.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Blend With Input
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls15\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Composite the generated details over the original footage.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Support adjustable Screen and Add blending where appropriate.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Provide an Input Blend control.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Preserve the ability to use the effect over dark footage without unnecessarily brightening the entire image.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The generated signal should not automatically replace the original footage when the user selects an overlay/compositing mode.\
Keep background generation, noise intensity, and input blend as distinct operations.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 9. Adjustable Parameters\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Expose functional controls:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls16\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}Speckle Density
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls the overall number of generated bright particles and segments.\
\ls16\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	2.	}Horizontal Stretch
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls the horizontal length of generated elements.\
\ls16\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	3.	}Top Density Boost
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 increases the probability of speckles toward the upper edge.\
\ls16\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	4.	}Frame Density Variation
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls density changes between frames.\
\ls16\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	5.	}Luma Intensity
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls the brightness of generated speckles.\
\ls16\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	6.	}Contrast
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls separation between dark and bright details.\
\ls16\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	7.	}Segment Length Variation
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls irregularity in horizontal segment lengths.\
\ls16\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	8.	}Input Blend
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls contribution of the generated signal over original footage.\
\ls16\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	9.	}Blend Mode
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 supports the appropriate existing Screen/Add compositing behavior.\
\ls16\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	10.	}Animate With Time
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 enables or freezes temporal changes.\
\ls16\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	11.	}Animation Speed
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls temporal evolution.\
\ls16\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	12.	}Random Seed
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls reproducible procedural variation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Do not add duplicate controls if equivalent functionality already exists in the VHSart interface.\
All exposed controls must genuinely affect the rendered result.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 10. Initial Preset Values\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Create the dedicated preset:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

